SUMMARY:Green River Adventures Tubing Event 
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nWe are the **Sloth Hike Team of WNC**: “W
 e will get there when we get there.” We dare to go where the ‘real’ 
 hike groups don’t ***!!***\n***https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TQ8H4EK2v
 t4***\nWe are going tubing on the Green River\; Up to 12 ppl are welcome t
 o join me.\nFloat Distance: 4.5mile. Accum descent: all downstream\nCost: 
 $30 prepaid – online.\n**READ RSVP instructions carefully and follow ste
 ps EXACTLY..\;-)**\n**READ Description below….**\nDrive time: 0.5 hrs 1-
 way\n**Return Not earlier than: 3PM (3-4 hrs on the river)**\nCarpool cont
 ributions appreciated. $3.00 suggested\nWeather Check: Saluda\, NC\nWeathe
 r cancellations will be posted at 6:30am.\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL BE ADDED
  AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\nWe currently have 7 driver(s) (=20ppl)\n**RSVP Instr
 uctions:**\nFirst: RSVP on HFF MeetUp to attend this event.\nSecond: Watch
  for notification on Wednesday morning\, August 5\, to go online to regist
 er and pay.\nWhen you register\, you will be able to choose the type of tu
 be you want to use. (single standard\, ergonomic or double tubes)\nYou wil
 l choose the 4.5 mile option and then pay online ($30). The link for more 
 information about the experience and to register is:\nhttps://greenriverad
 ventures.com/adventure/tube-green-river/\nLocation of start point: Riversi
 de Outpost\, 5476 Green River Cove Rd\, Saluda\, NC 28773.\nWe suggest sli
 ghtly open windows while carpooling. Only you know your own health status 
 so judge accordingly if an event may endanger your health or the health of
  others.\nPlease bring an extra pair of shoes to avoid bringing your muddy
  shoes into the driver's car at the end of the hike.\n**THIS IS -NOT- A DO
 G-PARTICIPANT EVENT.**\n**DESCRIPTION\;**\nRemember - hikes led by ‘the 
 Curmudgeon’ tend to have challenging surprises.\nWater nymphs tickle\, t
 ry not to laugh too hard – they scare easily.\nPack a snack/lunch and dr
 ink in waterproof bag to keep with you while tubing. We can leave keys at 
 the check-in site. If you bring your phone\, put it in a waterproof bag wi
 th a lariat. Wear water shoes that will stay secure on your feet! If water
  is low\, we may be walking part of the river. Sunscreen (???)\n**Tube the
  Green River in single standard\, ergonomic or double tubes.** Green River
  Tubing will handle the gear and logistics\, while you enjoy this mellow r
 iver with **occasional Class II rapids**. 4.5-mile option (3-4hrs). This t
 rip starts at the Riverside Outpost located at 5476 Green River Cove Rd\, 
 Saluda. **Please note that river levels vary daily and are rain dependent.
  We’re having fun no matter the conditions!**\nAll hikes are at your own
  risk. You are responsible for your OWN safety and adequate equipment.\nWa
 iver: : The organizer of this event is a volunteer and not a professional 
 guide. The function of the organizer is only to organize this event. There
  are certain risks inherent in any outdoor activity. Each participant\, by
  signing up to attend this event\, agrees to release from liability the le
 ader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Partners\, Affiliates\, and members for 
 any accident\, injury\, illness\, or personal loss which might occur while
  participating in this activity or while traveling in any vehicle during t
 his trip. **Each participant further agrees to abide by the rules and regu
 lations concerning safety\, to follow instructions of the leader(s)\, and 
 not to become intentionally separated from the group.** The leader(s) also
  has the right to use any images collected on this trip for recording on w
 ebsite photo collections.\ngordie's contact: CurmudgeonHiker@gmail.com\n(*
 *before** day of hike): 828.393.0297 (text only)\n**Pics: https://www.flic
 kr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums**
