SUMMARY:Fletcher Park
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\n**A WALK IN THE PARK\,**\nWe will Tour de P
 arks of the area. One at a time.\n**THIS WEEK: *BILL MOORE COMMUNITY PARK 
 (AKA FLETCHER PARK):***\nWe are the **Sloth Walking Team**: “We will get
  there when we get there.”\nPat M will lead this event. Up to 12 ppl are
  welcome to join us.\n**https://biggeekdad.com/2015/11/nature-rx/**\nLengt
 h: 2 mi\; Total ascent: 0.0 ft\nDifficulty: easy\, peasy. In & Out natural
  packed surface.\nSuitable for beginners? yes\n**Return Not earlier than: 
 11:30 am**\n**Optional:** Lunch somewhere???\nWeather Check: Fletcher\, NC
 \nWeather cancellations will be posted at 6:30am.\nThis is a dog-participa
 nt walk. This event is NOT for those who are uncomfortable with the antics
  of fun-loving dogs. 'On leash' rules apply.\nDESCRIPTION\;\n**Due to rece
 nt events\, Ouija boards are no longer permitted.**\nFletcher Community Pa
 rk is recognized as one of the best family parks in Western North Carolina
 . Park patrons have access to scenic walking trails\, Cane Creek\, and cou
 ntless other amenities.\nAll walks are at your own risk. You are responsib
 le for your OWN safety and adequate equipment.\nWaiver: : The organizer of
  this event is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The function of t
 he organizer is only to organize this event. There are certain risks inher
 ent in any outdoor activity. Each participant\, by signing up to attend th
 is event\, agrees to release from liability the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Frie
 nds\, its Partners\, Affiliates\, and members for any accident\, injury\, 
 illness\, or personal loss which might occur while participating in this a
 ctivity or while traveling in any vehicle during this trip. Each participa
 nt further agrees to abide by the rules and regulations concerning safety\
 , to follow instructions of the leader(s)\, and not to become intentionall
 y separated from the group. The leader(s) also has the right to use any im
 ages collected on this trip for recording on website photo collections.\ng
 ordie's contact: CurmudgeonHiker@gmail.com\n(**before** day of hike): 828.
 393.0297 (text only)\n**Pics: https://www.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/
 albums**
