SUMMARY:UnRuffle yo’self at Big Hungry River Cascades
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nWe are the **Sloth Hike Team of WNC**: “W
 e will get there when we get there.” We dare to go where the ‘real’ 
 hike groups don’t ***!!***\nI am going to unravel my stress at the casca
 des of Big Hungry River near Saluda. Up to 12 ppl are welcome to join me.\
 n**[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TQ8H4EK2vt4](https://www.youtube.com/w
 atch?v=TQ8H4EK2vt4)**\n**This is a designated ‘silent’ Relaxation Hike
 \; we will engage quiet for the day. But "Ooh's and Aah's" are encouraged.
 **\nI will spend up to 2 hours at the falls water-immersion-ing\, eating\,
  reading and pretending to meditate.\n**Hike Details:**\nHike Distance: ½
  mile Accum **descent**: 50 ft\nPace: **1.5mph – because I’m an ol’ 
 Codger.**\nDifficulty: Steep\, rocky descent to the river. Boulders line t
 he water.\nOptional: Bring a lite-weight campchair and/or innertube.\n**OP
 TIONAL:** Water immersion available\; be prepared.\nDrive time: 20 min/ 6 
 miles (1-way)\n**Return Not earlier than:** : 1:30PM **(=3.0 hrs)**\nCarpo
 ol contributions appreciated. $2.00 suggested\nWeather Check: Saluda\, NC\
 nWeather cancellations will be posted at 6:30am.\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL B
 E ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\n(I currently have 1.5 driver(s). (=8ppl)\nWe 
 suggest masks and open windows while carpooling. Only you know your own he
 alth status so judge accordingly if an event may endanger your health or t
 he health of others.\nPlease bring an extra pair of shoes to avoid bringin
 g your muddy shoes into the driver's car at the end of the hike.\nIncessan
 t prattlers will be assumed to be having an affair. Obstreperous raucous y
 awping is discouraged.\n**THIS IS A DOG-PARTICIPANT HIKE.** This event is 
 NOT for those who are uncomfortable with the antics of fun-loving dogs.\nW
 ell trained dogs (you don’t have to yell.) can be 'off-leash'. 'On leash
 ' during the Unraveling (‘Cept when swimmin’). Small (lap)dogs may car
 pool. Large dogs will drive themselves.\n**DESCRIPTION\;**\nRemember - hik
 es led by ‘the Curmudgeon’ tend to have challenging surprises.\nForest
 ed riverside boulders. Water flow is ‘wade-able’.\nOptional: water-imm
 ersion-ing\n**Due to recent events\, Ouija boards are no longer permitted.
 **\nWe will spend up to 2 hrs at the Falls. Come prepared to meditate\, pr
 actice your Tai-Chi\, **森林浴**\, read a book\, prepare a meal\, play 
 a flute.\n**UnRavel:** To experience a time of quiet in a manner that you 
 feel worthwhile.\nEngage the 5 senses (sight\, smell\, touch\, taste\, hea
 ring)\,\nObserve the movement of the forest & water.\nBreathe the aroma of
  the air\, water\, plants and forest.\nFeel the texture of the air\, water
 \, trees and plants.\nListening to the sound of air\, water\, critters & b
 irds\;\nTaste the air of the breezes or soothing snacks.\nWaiver: The orga
 nizer of this event is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The funct
 ion of the organizer is only to organize this event. There are certain ris
 ks inherent in any outdoor activity. Each participant\, by signing up to a
 ttend this event\, agrees to release from liability the leader(s)\, Hendo 
 Fun Friends\, its Partners\, Affiliates\, and members for any accident\, i
 njury\, illness\, or personal loss which might occur while participating i
 n this activity or while traveling in any vehicle during this trip. **Each
  participant further agrees to abide by the rules and regulations concerni
 ng safety\, to follow instructions of the leader(s)\, and not to become in
 tentionally separated from the group.** The leader(s) also has the right t
 o use any images collected on this trip for recording on website photo col
 lections.\ngordie's contact: curmudgeonhiker@gmail.com\n(**before** day of
  hike): 828.393.0297 (talk & text)
